  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "label": "Rename a function",
      "prompt": "Rename getUser to fetchUser everywhere in the repo.",
      "needs": [
        "grep",
        "edit_file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t2",
      "label": "Change a signature",
      "prompt": "Add a required `locale` argument to formatPrice and update every caller.",
      "needs": [
        "grep",
        "edit_file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t3",
      "label": "Remove a flag",
      "prompt": "Delete the ENABLE_LEGACY_CHECKOUT flag and the code paths behind it.",
      "needs": [
        "grep",
        "edit_file"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "actions": {
    "grep": {
      "kind": "tool",
      "tool": "grep",
      "text": "grep(\"getUser\\\\(\")  → 7 matches in 4 files",
      "tokens": 700
    },
    "edit": {
      "kind": "tool",
      "tool": "edit_file",
      "text": "edit_file(\"src/api/users.ts\", \"getUser(\", \"fetchUser(\")  (and 3 more files)",
      "tokens": 400
    },
    "test": {
      "kind": "tool",
      "tool": "run_tests",
      "text": "run_tests()  → 312 passed",
      "tokens": 500
    },
    "tangent": {
      "kind": "think",
      "text": "While I'm here, I could also tidy up the imports in this file...",
      "tokens": 250
    },
    "done": {
      "kind": "answer",
      "correct": true,
      "text": "Renamed getUser to fetchUser in 4 files (7 call sites). Type check and tests pass."
    },
    "done_early": {
      "kind": "answer",
      "correct": false,
      "text": "Done. Renamed getUser to fetchUser in src/api/users.ts and its callers."
    }
  },
  "policy": {
    "base": {
      "grep": 4,
      "edit": 0,
      "test": 0,
      "tangent": 0,
      "done": 0,
      "done_early": 0
    },
    "modifiers": [
      {
        "when": {
          "called": "grep"
        },
        "shift": {
          "edit": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "setting": "model.temperature",
          "op": ">",
          "value": 0.5
        },
        "shift": {
          "tangent": 0.6
        },
        "note": "High temperature samples the less likely next steps more often."
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "state": "ready"
        },
        "set": {
          "done": 3,
          "done_early": 0.5
        }
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "all": [
            {
              "state": "ready"
            },
            {
              "setting": "model.temperature",
              "op": ">",
              "value": 0.5
            }
          ]
        },
        "shift": {
          "done_early": 0.6
        }
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "all": [
            {
              "state": "ready"
            },
            {
              "setting": "model.temperature",
              "op": "<=",
              "value": 0.2
            }
          ]
        },
        "scale": {
          "done_early": 0.6
        },
        "note": "Temperature 0 narrows the spread but does not remove the mistake the model is most likely to make."
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "all": [
            {
              "state": "ready"
            },
            {
              "tool": "run_tests"
            },
            {
              "not": {
                "called": "run_tests"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "shift": {
          "test": 12
        }
      },
      {
        "when": {
          "called": "run_tests"
        },
        "scale": {
          "done_early": 0.1
        },
        "shift": {
          "done": 3
        },
        "note": "A failing type check tells the model exactly which call site it missed."
      }
    ]
  },
  "goals": [
    {
      "id": "pass",
      "label": "Pass at least 95% of 150 runs",
      "metric": "success_rate",
      "op": ">=",
      "value": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Run it and scroll through a few failing runs. The input is identical every time. What differs is which step the model sampled.",
    "Turning the temperature down helps, but not enough on its own: the model's most likely mistake is still likely at temperature 0.",
    "Set temperature to 0 and give the agent a deterministic check: a run_tests tool wired to the loop. (A Judge node also works, at extra cost per run.)"
  ],
  "explain": "Lower temperature shrinks the spread of what the model does; a deterministic check (tests, a type checker, a schema) catches what is left. Together they turn a coin-flip CI job into a signal."
}